# MC-X-F10: a fill whose demand is an adjustment's -a.change. The prelude kind adjustments has the attribute change,
# "δ, signed, of the leg's type" (L §5.14.3): its unit is the adjusted leg's, per value (a transfers leg is `cash:
# any`), so load can't see it. L §5.12: "A fill's supply and demand share one unit, which may be any"; L §3.2: "The run
# checks the keys load couldn't see, as load checks two currencies"; L §8.4: refused at load where the types show it,
# otherwise at the key. v2 (known 2027-03-15) lowers amt from 100 to 90 for the three months booked before it: three
# adjustments of -10.00 PLN (L §5.14.3), dated 2027-03-15, each taken from 2027-04, the first month after it in
# `order m` (L §5.12 Take). snap11 refused the fill at load: LOAD-UNIT supply (money PLN) and demand (dyn).
# L5_12_fill_dynamic_unit_run: the same fill over a leg in EUR is refused at the take (RUN-DOMAIN).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2027-06-30
  start 2027-01-01
  end 2027-06-30
source src "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place acct: accounts PLN lives 2027-01-01..
place office: outside lives 2027-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
move pay[m in months]: transfers
  on start_of(m)
  leg cash from office to acct amount amt
fill wh
  supply amt for m in months
  demand -a.change for a in adjustments over .. where a.adjusts in transfers and a.change < 0
  arc a.day < start_of(m)
  order m
version v
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2026-12-31
  amt = 100
ask t: wh.taken[m, a] for m in months, a in adjustments over .. where m == month_of(a.day) + 1 or m == month_of(a.day)
ask d: sum(-a.change for a in adjustments over ..)
version v2
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2027-03-15
  replace amt = 90
=== expect
d: 30.00 PLN
  cut 2027-06-30
t (m = 2027-03, a = adjustments[pay[2027-01].cash, v2]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2027-06-30
t (m = 2027-03, a = adjustments[pay[2027-02].cash, v2]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2027-06-30
t (m = 2027-03, a = adjustments[pay[2027-03].cash, v2]): 0.00 PLN
  cut 2027-06-30
t (m = 2027-04, a = adjustments[pay[2027-01].cash, v2]): 10.00 PLN
  cut 2027-06-30
t (m = 2027-04, a = adjustments[pay[2027-02].cash, v2]): 10.00 PLN
  cut 2027-06-30
t (m = 2027-04, a = adjustments[pay[2027-03].cash, v2]): 10.00 PLN
  cut 2027-06-30
